WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.326
Part two.

00:00:01.326 --> 00:00:04.654
Play it back: loops, sequences and schedules.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.490
Our Buy a book scenario is ready in the list.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.418
Click Play, and let Pocket QA do the rest.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.385
It plays right on the page.

00:00:14.385 --> 00:00:19.872
The little panel in the corner shows the current step, with a Stop button always at hand.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.436
The toolbar badge counts along too, so you can follow the run with the popup closed.

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:25.464
Done.

00:00:25.464 --> 00:00:31.343
The Last run card says Finished, no checks: every step ran, but nothing was checked yet.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:32.713
Need it more than once?

00:00:32.713 --> 00:00:35.872
Set a loop count, with a pause between rounds.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.329
Only need part of it?

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:43.072
Click a step's number: play from it, up to it, or just that one step.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.783
And Run as plays it like a phone, or on a slow network: an iPhone 14 on 3G, for example.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.674
Or chain several scenarios into one run.

00:00:53.674 --> 00:00:59.659
I've prepared a second one, Update profile, which uploads an avatar and picks from a dropdown.

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:03.622
Start the sequence.

00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:08.054
The two scenarios run back to back, and the popup shows which one is playing.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:17.989
File pickers and native dropdowns don't stop it either.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:24.000
Both are done: the avatar is uploaded, and the favourite category is set.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.503
Finally, schedules.

00:01:25.503 --> 00:01:28.654
Pick the scenario, a time and a start page.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:42.387
Tick Repeat daily to run it every day, then click Add.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.557
Now we wait for the scheduled time.

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:55.724
Right on time, Pocket QA opens the start page in a new tab and runs the scenario.

00:01:55.724 --> 00:01:57.663
Nobody has to click a thing.

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.677
Playing back is easy.

00:02:02.677 --> 00:02:04.455
But how do we know the result is right?

00:02:04.455 --> 00:02:05.796
That comes next.
